<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gateway compatibility="1" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="http://schema.itrsgroup.com/GA7.12.1-261009/gateway.xsd">
    <!-- Full-day local-time overrides. Annual dates (DD/MM) precede dated exceptions (DD/MM/YYYY).
See holiday-calendars-sa.md for South America coverage and source confidence.
Confidence varies by calendar and source format; it is not a guarantee of accuracy or completeness. -->
	<activeTimes>
		<activeTimeGroup name="Layer 0 - Holidays">
			<activeTimeGroup name="Layer 0 - SA - Brazil">
                <!-- Brazil calendars, sorted with public holidays before collective leave and exchanges.
Named calendars retain their own scope and timezone; a group is not a business-hours schedule.
Confidence varies by calendar; see the source comments and holiday-calendars-sa.md. -->
				<activeTime name="Holidays - BR B3 Listed Equities - Exchange">
                    <!-- Gathered: 2026-11-20

Confidence: Medium - official human-readable exchange calendar;
market-specific footnotes and full-day closures require interpretation.

Sources:
- https://www.b3.com.br/en_us/solutions/platforms/puma-trading-system/for-members-and-traders/trading-calendar/holidays/ (B3 market calendar)

Notes:
The public holiday calendar is not encoded. Use the B3 calendar only for
listed equities, not as a substitute for public holidays.

Timezone: America/Sao_Paulo. Listed equity closures only; not a public
holiday, FX or settlement calendar.

Santiago, Bogotá and Buenos Aires are also candidates for South America if those
markets are monitored; no calendars are encoded for them. -->
					<scheduledPeriod><date>01/01/2026</date><override>true</override></scheduledPeriod>
					<scheduledPeriod><date>16/02/2026</date><override>true</override></scheduledPeriod>
					<scheduledPeriod><date>17/02/2026</date><override>true</override></scheduledPeriod>
					<scheduledPeriod><date>03/04/2026</date><override>true</override></scheduledPeriod>
